// The guide Novourq Cloud AI reads in every chat so it can answer any "where do I...?" or "how does it...?" question
// about the platform. Pages and skills are built from the same lists the app itself uses, so the guide stays current.
import { STAFF_HUBS } from './staffHubs'
import { WORKFLOWS } from './ai-workflows'
import { TAB_DESCRIPTIONS } from './tab-descriptions'

const HOW_TO = `
HOW THINGS WORK (answer from this; give the exact click path)
- Where do I go? sits at the top of Real Estate Intelligence: pick a task such as Add a tenant, Check a tenant’s ID and income, Add a guest booking or Chase rent and press the area that fits. Property Management means we manage the property for the landlord, Estate Agency means we let or sell it for the landlord, Vacation Rentals means guest bookings. Hover an area name anywhere on the page to see what it means. Limits: it opens the page, it does not add the record for you, and it only shows the areas your role can open.
- Get started checklist: a new account sees it at the top of Real Estate Intelligence with four steps, choose your currency, add your first property, add the landlord who owns it, add a tenant. Press Open on a step to go to the right page. Steps tick off by themselves once a record exists, and the box disappears when all three are done. Press Hide to hide it on this device. Limits: it counts records across Property Management, Estate Agency and Vacation Rentals and only shows steps your role can open.
- Property allowance: every paying client's plan includes 3 properties. A Property Management and Estate Agency property is one property (they are the same property in both), and each Vacation Rentals property counts too; properties moved to Former do not count. On the 4th, Add property shows 'Add more properties': each extra property is £12 a month, added to the NOVOURQ subscription in Stripe and charged pro rata for the rest of the billing period (or from the end of the free trial), and the property is then added straight away. The counter beside Properties shows used / allowed. Only an admin can buy extras. Lifetime clients cannot buy extras themselves yet; our team adds them. Removing extras is done by contacting support. Internal NOVOURQ accounts are unlimited.
- Your plan and billing: Settings → Payments, the Your NOVOURQ plan box at the top (account owner only). If you cancel through Manage billing, the box says when the plan ends and that you keep full access until then. It shows the plan (Monthly £49 a month, Annual £470.40 a year, or Lifetime £175.50 one-time), the status, and during the free trial the days left and the date of the first payment. Manage billing opens a secure Stripe page to update the card, see invoices, switch plan or cancel. Lifetime plans have no Manage billing because nothing more is due. Team members who are not the account owner do not see the box.
- Currency: Settings → Currency (admin only). Same page: choose your company time zone (UK, Ireland, Central Europe, UAE, Jamaica, US or Canada zones). It decides what today is for overdue invoices and rent, due dates, compliance expiry, Finance alerts and the dashboard; it starts on UK time. Pick the symbol your company uses, pound, US dollar, Jamaican dollar, euro, UAE dirham or Canadian dollar, and press Save. Rent, income, costs and totals across Property Management, Estate Agency, Vacation Rentals, Developments and At a glance then show that symbol. Limits: it only changes the symbol, amounts are shown exactly as entered and nothing is converted, Unit Profit and the plan prices stay in pounds, and the AI’s own reports still show pounds. Landlord and tenant portals show the symbol of the company they belong to. New invoices start in your currency and you can switch each one to pound, US dollar, Jamaican dollar, euro, UAE dirham or Canadian dollar; the overdue rent email, landlord statements and the tenant and landlord data summary use your symbol. Marketing budgets, Vendors invoices and CRM deal values also use this symbol.
- NOVOURQ mobile app (iPhone and Android, coming to the App Store and Google Play): one login for everyone, and the app shows the views that match the email address. Guests see their stay, Wi-Fi, directions and house guide. Tenants see rent, payments, documents and can report repairs. Landlords (Owner) see payouts, statements and maintenance. Partners see their investment, returns and updates. Co-hosts see the properties assigned to them, their bookings, earnings and maintenance (read only), from their own Co-hosts record. Companies using NOVOURQ (the account owner, Admins and Co Founders) get a Business view of Novourq Cloud AI: chats handled and AI actions in the last 7 days, customer chats that need a person to follow up, and what is waiting in Approvals. Staff see Today, Tasks and Enquiries. A person with more than one role switches under Account. Limits: the app only reads and reports; approving AI actions, anything that sends money and legal contracts are always done in the portal (Novourq Cloud AI, Approvals), co-hosts and businesses only ever see their own company's records, and Delete my account in the app only removes the app login.
- Free trial countdown: while a company is on its 14-day free trial, a small box at the bottom of the left menu, just above the person's name, shows how many days are left (it turns amber at 3 days or fewer, and shows 'Trial ends today' on the last day). Hover it to see the end date. It disappears once the plan is paid or after a lifetime purchase. If someone asks, the trial is billed automatically at the end unless they cancel before it ends.
- Menu: the left menu is the NOVOURQ Ecosystem. It holds Dashboard, Real Estate Intelligence, Novourq Cloud AI, then the Human Intelligence Hub. Help Centre and Settings sit just under the Human Intelligence Hub. The Help Centre has short video walkthroughs of each part of Novourq (Getting started, Real Estate Intelligence, Novourq Cloud AI, Human Intelligence Hub, Map and 3D walk-through, Settings, Packs, links and onboarding, Agent programme, Website links and careers, Your plan and currency, Co-hosts, crew and HR) and the step-by-step guide. The videos are widescreen (16:9) with the steps written beside the screen. It is open to everyone except investor partners. In Settings: My Account, Team Management, Payments, System Messages (news from us), Submissions (report an issue or bug, leave a review or suggest an idea, and see our replies) AI Authority (admins choose what the AI does automatically, what waits for a person, and what is off), Phone Assistant (admins link their own mobile, then message or voice-note Novourq Cloud AI on WhatsApp to ask about the portfolio or add tasks) Privacy & Data (admins download all company data as a file, or request account deletion).
- Meetings booking link: on the Meetings page the Client booking link is your company's own (it ends in ?code=...). Share it; anyone who sends a request appears under New request on your own Meetings board, you get a bell notification and email, they are added to your CRM, and they get a confirmation email with your company name. Each company's link only reaches that company.
- Tax Compliance: admins only. Each client has their own company here; open its tab and press Edit details to change the company name, currency, registration status, company number and tax note. Banks, obligations and intercompany transfers are added on the same page. Nothing is filed or paid from here.
- Company name: texts, marketing emails, signing links and documents use the company name set in Invoice settings; if none is set they say Property Management Team, so set it first.
- Earnings checker (Landlord Leads): Staff Centre → Landlord Leads → Link & embed code gives your company's own checker link (it ends in ?code=...) and website embed code. A landlord fills in the form, gets an estimate by email signed with your company name, and the lead lands in Landlord Leads and your CRM with a bell alert. Their 'Book a call' button opens your own meeting booking link. Each company's link only reaches that company.
- Finance currency: Staff Centre → Finance shows money in and out, owner payouts and rent roll in your company currency (set in Settings → Currency). Amounts in other currencies (pound, US dollar, Jamaican dollar, euro, dirham, Canadian dollar) are converted at today's rate, shown under Exchange rates used.
- Exchange Rates and Unit Profit: Real Estate Intelligence → Property Management → Exchange Rates. Each property has a currency (pound, US dollar, Jamaican dollar, euro, dirham or Canadian dollar). Enter how many of your company currency one unit of another currency is worth; Unit Profit and totals then convert into your company currency (Settings → Currency). Head rent is taken as your company currency.
- Novourq Cloud AI: ask it in plain words (typing or the mic). It reads today's records you can see (rent, leases ending, maintenance, compliance, check-ins, invoices) and answers from them, drafts messages for you to send, and cannot change anything itself.
- Clock in and late arrivals (part of Work Hours): every staff member and account owner has a Clock in / Clock out button at the top of Work Hours and on the Dashboard next to Work hours today. Signing in to the portal does not clock anyone in; they press Clock in to start and Clock out to finish, and it shows hours so far. The account owner (and staff they choose under Who can see this) sees Clock-ins and late arrivals on Work Hours: each clock-in with shift, time in, time out, hours and On time or Late N min, a Late arrivals count, hours clocked, and a red line naming anyone who has a shift today and has not clocked in once their grace period has passed. Press Set shift times (account owner only) to give each person a start time, a grace period in minutes (default 5) and working days (default Mon to Fri); times use the time zone of the computer the owner saves from. Someone with no shift set is never flagged late. A clock-in left open for 18 hours is shown as Not clocked out. Download (CSV) exports clock-ins for payroll. Preview example shows sample figures. Missed clock-in email: the account owner is emailed when someone with a shift today has not clocked in 15 minutes after it starts (checked every 10 minutes, once per person per day, and not more than 3 hours after the shift start). Limits: it records the button presses, not what someone does away from the portal.
- Work Hours: Staff Centre, Human Intelligence Hub, Team, Work Hours (account owner only, plus staff the owner chooses). Shows each person's sign-in time, sign-out time, time on the portal and active time, and the pages they opened, by date range, with totals per person and a CSV download for payroll. The Dashboard also has a Work hours today box next to New applicants at the bottom (today's sign-ins, sign-outs and time, plus the last 7 days); only the owner sees it unless they press Who can see this and tick staff. It records staff and account owners only, from the moment this feature went live. Signing out with the Sign out button records the exact time; if someone closes the tab or goes quiet for 15 minutes, it ends at the last time they were seen. It shows portal use, not what they do offline.
- Automation by area: on the Dashboard, each area is one row with a progress bar and an All on or number off tag. Click a row to see its automations (green is on, grey is off), or use Expand all and Show only off. Switching skills on or off is done in Manage skills.
- Dashboard video: on the Dashboard, the NOVOURQ Walk video (showcasing our new AI technology) sits beside the Property map; Portfolio Performance and What Novourq Cloud AI did are the same size below, with Automation by area full width under them. Press play to watch; it does not start by itself.
- Jamaica real estate charges: Staff Centre → Client Properties → Deal Analyser (you need the Invest module). When a purchase or land deal is in Jamaica (currency J$, or the address says Jamaica), a Jamaica real estate charges card appears under the form and again with the results. Purchaser pays shows stamp duty, agreement for sale, GCT, registration, attorney's fee, GCT on the attorney's fee and letter of possession, plus a Surveyor's fee box for your own quote, and adds the 6.00% mortgage cost only when you are buying with a mortgage. Vendor pays shows the seller's costs, including transfer tax and the 5.00% commission. Every percentage and flat fee can be changed for the deal you are looking at and is kept with the deal; an admin can press Save my changes as company rates so every deal starts from the company's own rates, and Reset company rates to standard. Each company has its own rates. Limits: the amounts are approximate, flat fees are in J$ shown at a rough exchange rate, and it is not legal or tax advice. Not shown for rent-to-rent deals.
- Market intelligence panels: on the Dashboard, under Today's schedule, four panels for people who have the Invest module. Featured Property Analysis shows your saved deal with the best yield (price, monthly rent, gross yield) and links to Human Intelligence Hub → Client Properties → Deal Analyser → Saved Deals. Top Locations by Rental Yield ranks the places in your saved deals by average gross yield, with tabs for your busiest areas and a month-on-month change once a place has deals in two months. My Watchlist shows your first four watchlist properties and links to Human Intelligence Hub → Client Properties → Watchlist. Quick Insights (AI) is a few plain sentences Novourq Cloud AI writes from the same saved deals and watchlist (refreshed once a day, or press Refresh); it adds no outside market figures, and Open market check goes to the Deal Analyser where the Local market check lives. Only deals saved with a purchase price and a rent have a yield, so rent-to-rent deals do not appear in the yield panels. Press Preview example to see the panels filled with labelled example figures that are not your data; press it again to return to yours.
- Property no longer managed: in Real Estate Intelligence, Properties (long lets and short stays together) and in Vacation Rentals, Properties, each property has a No longer managed button. It asks for the date it stopped being the company's, a reason (Owner took it back, Contract ended, Sold, Lease not renewed or Other) and an optional note. The property then leaves the active lists, counts, the website and booking page, calendar syncs and the AI, but all its bookings, rent, documents and history are kept. Former properties show under the Former filter in Real Estate Intelligence, Properties (and a Former properties list at the bottom of Vacation Rentals, Properties), each with a Restore button. Restoring does not switch the website listing back on. A long let and its Estate Agency record are one property, so ending one ends both. Future bookings and open jobs are not cancelled automatically. Admins, Co Founders and the property teams can do this. It is different from Delete, which erases the property for good.
- Signing documents with initials and dates: in Staff Centre, Documents, open a template and press + Initials box or + Date box where the signer must initial a section or pick a date (also + Insert blank for anything else). When you send it, the client opens the link on their phone, works through each box with a progress bar and a Fill my initials shortcut, then draws or types a signature and presses Finish and sign. The signed PDF shows signature, initials, dates, time and IP, is emailed to both sides, and for an owner or tenant is filed automatically in their Documents (and their portal). You can fill dates yourself before sending.
- Head lease documents: in Real Estate Intelligence, Head Leases, press Documents on a lease (shows how many of the 5 key documents are filled). Upload the master lease agreement, head lessor documents, landlord ID (with its expiry date), proof of ownership and change of electricity papers, plus any other files, as PDF, Word or photo up to 15 MB. Files are private to your company and open through links that last 5 minutes. Admins, Co Founders and property teams only. Landlord ID shows a warning 90 days before it expires. Owners and Tenants: press Documents on an owner or tenant for the same checklist (owners: ID, proof of ownership, management agreement, proof of address, bank details; tenants: tenancy agreement, ID, right to rent, proof of income, references). Each file is marked In portal or Staff only, and In portal files show automatically in that owner's Documents tab or that tenant's Documents tab, with a note of what is still needed. Estate Agency owners and tenants work the same way (Estate Agency, Landlords and Tenants, press Documents) and show in the Estate Agency portals. Document hub: owners and tenants can upload their own files in the portal Documents tab (Take photo or upload) and see a progress bar and what is still needed. Their uploads wait in Staff Centre, Documents, under To review, where you press View, Approve or Reject (a reason is required and is emailed to them). Rejected files show them why so they can upload again. Under Still missing documents, tick people and press Ask selected (or Chase on one person, or Ask them for missing documents inside a Documents window) to email what is missing with a link to their portal. After the first ask, reminders go out automatically every 3 days, up to 5, until they finish; people who were never asked get none. Reminders and asks need email set up and the person to have an email address. Old tenant files: in Property Management, Tenants, a Move to private button appears while older tenant files sit in the open All files list; it moves them (admins and Co Founders, 25 at a time) into each tenant's private Documents, keeping In portal choices. Lease signing: tenancy and lease sign pages now also ask the signer to initial the term, rent, deposit and contract sections before signing. Secure link: in an owner's or tenant's Documents window press Email secure link (sends them an email) or Get link and WhatsApp text (copy the link or the ready-made message into WhatsApp). The link opens a private page with no login that shows contracts to sign, documents to upload (take a photo or upload), invoices and rent to pay by card, and files you shared. It works for 14 days; a new press gives a fresh link. Templates accept a Word (.docx) or a PDF: Staff Centre, Documents, Templates, open a template, press Upload Word or PDF (admins only). A PDF is read as text, up to 4 MB, and turned into headings and paragraphs you can edit, so check the wording and layout after; a scanned PDF (a picture of pages) has no text and is refused, use the Word version instead. Automatic rules: on the Documents page press Automatic rules (admins change them). Add a rule by choosing when something happens (new tenant added, tenancy created, booking confirmed, client property signed, partner paid, rent 7 days late, lease ends in 60 days) and which template to send, then switch it on. It only acts on events after it is switched on, sends each document once, needs email set up and an email address for the person, is checked daily, and Run now checks straight away. Templates: press Templates at the top of the Documents page. Landlord agreements (Master Lease, Landlord Property Management Agreement, Co-Host agreements) open for the signer in the NOVOURQ form layout: logo at the top, navy headings, a ruled line to fill in beside each label, tick boxes for choices, and your contact line at the bottom. Every contract and letter now uses this same look on the signing page, and the PDF copy (download and emailed signed copy) matches it: the NOVOURQ artwork as the page background (no corner logo), navy uppercase headings, a ruled fill-in line beside each blank, tick boxes for choices, and a footer rule with your contact line and Page X of Y. Offer letters keep the NOVOURQ background artwork. Add landlord templates (Documents, Templates, admins) adds the Shortlet Landlord Agreement, Landlord Onboarding (up to 4 landlords, one after another) and Estate Agency Property Management Agreement in your PDF wording; it never changes a template you already have. Property features are typed in one box rather than ticked. Email me test contracts (same place, admins) sends a [TEST] copy of every Agreements template to your own email so you can open the signing link and try signing. Novourq Voice (spoken or phone) can do the same when an admin says, for example, send me the test contracts or send me a test Master Lease; they only ever send to the admin’s own email. Before a document is sent, staff are warned if company details such as Company address, Work location or the signer’s role are still empty, and can fill them in or send anyway. Limits: the layout follows the template wording, so edit the template to change what is asked; each company has its own: its own templates, logo, name, contact line, offer letter email and page background. Add landlord templates and Add HR templates give a client the same templates in its own company name, with blanks for the address, website and portal; the fee amounts and wording are NOVOURQ’s, so each client edits them for their own business. A company with no background set gets a plain white page with its logo. Sending a document for signing: Staff Centre → Human Intelligence Hub → Clients and sales → Owners & Tenants → Documents → Send a document. Pick a template, then the person (or type their name and email), fill in the company details such as Company address, Work location and the signer’s role, and send. They get an email with their own signing link; it needs no login and works on a phone. On the signing page they fill in the blanks themselves (an employee fills in their own home address and the signing date), tick boxes for choices, then sign. When they sign, they and you get the signed PDF by email, and the document shows as Signed in Documents. Each kind of document shows its own department’s email in the footer and replies go there. NOVOURQ: offer letters, employment contracts and staff notices use career@thenovourq.com; tenancy agreements and tenant signing invitations use leasing@; landlord and owner agreements (Master Lease, Landlord Property Management, Co-Host, Shortlet, Estate Agency, Landlord Onboarding) use clientrelations@; payslips and payroll use finance@; invoices use billing@; legal notices use legal@; anything else uses admin@; marketing uses hello@ and general public enquiries contact.us@ (all @thenovourq.com). Each paying company sets its own address for each kind, and its own contract page background, in Staff Centre → Invoices → Invoice settings → Documents (admins); a kind left blank keeps that company’s normal contact details, and NOVOURQ’s addresses never show for another company. Emails are still sent from the portal’s notification address; only the footer and reply-to change. Marketing emails are sent from the marketing address (hello@ for NOVOURQ) unless a Send from mailbox is chosen, and replies are still tracked by the portal. The meeting booking confirmation replies to the general enquiries address (contact.us@ for NOVOURQ); demo requests for NOVOURQ alert contact.us@thenovourq.com. Every other document uses the company’s normal contact details. Any wording change to a contract waits for admin approval first. Landlord agreements, offer letters and the other contracts all come out in the same NOVOURQ look. To try a contract yourself, press Email me test contracts (Documents → Templates) or ask Novourq Voice. Utilities tracker: Real Estate Intelligence, Operations, Utilities has two views. Tracker shows each property as cards, one per bill account such as electricity (JPS) and internet (Flow), with the latest bill, the change on the last bill (marked high at 30 percent or more), paid, due or overdue status, a 12 bill chart, usage if you enter it, and an Open JPS or Open Flow button to the supplier's site. Press Add bill on a card to enter the amount, bill date, due date, usage and optionally the PDF or photo of the bill; Bills lists the history where you can mark paid or unpaid or delete. Owner sees and Tenant sees tick boxes decide who can see each account; owners are shown by default and tenants only when ticked. Accounts is the list where you add or edit an account (service, supplier, account number, monthly amount, next bill date). Owners see Utilities as a tab in their portal and tenants in theirs, read only, and on their secure link. Automatic bills: JPS and Flow have no feed we can connect to, but both email bills, so each bill account has its own bill inbox address (shown on its card, with a Copy button, in the form bills+code at the platform email domain). Set that address as the e-bill email on the JPS or Flow account, or set a forwarding rule in your email so each bill is forwarded to it. When a bill arrives, the amount, bill date, due date and usage are read from the email or its PDF or photo and added by themselves (marked From email), the next bill date updates, and you get a notification. A bill is not added, and you are told instead, when it is for a different account number, in a different currency, is not a bill, or cannot be read; add those by hand. Duplicates are skipped. Bills are not marked paid automatically. It needs inbound email set up (the same Resend inbound that handles replies) and the AI key. Finding it: Human Intelligence Hub, Clients and sales, Owners & Tenants, then the Documents tab along the top. New client link (for someone not in the system yet): Staff Centre, Documents, press New client link at the top. Choose owner or tenant, Property Management or Estate Agency, the contract they sign (a template that needs a signature, optional), and whether to ask for ID and documents, then press Create link and copy the link or the WhatsApp message. They open it on their phone, enter name, email, phone and property, upload documents, then read, initial and sign the contract. Their owner or tenant record is created as soon as they save their details (it may be left behind if they stop part way), their uploads wait in Documents under To review, the signed contract files itself in their Documents, and you get a notification. The list under Create link shows each link as Not opened, In progress, Finished or Expired. When you pick an agreement on the link it shows in their Documents step as Management agreement, Ready to sign, and they read and sign it in the next step; if you pick none it shows We'll add this and you add it yourself afterwards. The management agreement (owners) and tenancy agreement (tenants) are not something they upload: they show as We'll add this with no upload button, are not counted in their documents to do, and are left out of reminder emails. You add the generated contract yourself in the owner's or tenant's Documents window, or they sign it in the Sign step when you chose a contract on the link. Press Copy link beside any link not yet finished or expired to copy it again (the latest 20 are listed). Links last 14 days; anyone holding one can fill it in, so send it only to that person. A finished client can then be sent a secure link as usual. Contracts and invoices appear on it when they were sent to that person from Staff Centre, Documents or Finance, Invoices (pick the person from the list). Pay now by card needs Stripe connected under Settings, Payments, and the invoice marked as sent; paid invoices mark themselves paid, other invoices can still be paid by bank transfer. Chase and automatic reminder emails now use the secure link too. Anyone holding the link can see that person's documents until it expires, so send it only to them.
Electricity limit: on each electricity account card (Real Estate Intelligence, Operations, Utilities, Tracker) set Covered limit per bill, for example J$7,000 on furnished properties, press Save limit, or Apply to all electricity to set it on every electricity account. The card then shows a bar of what the company covers and what the tenant pays above the limit, and the tenant sees it as Your share in their portal. On a bill in the Bills list, Invoice tenant creates a draft invoice to the property's tenant for the part above the limit; review and send it from Invoices. Limits: one limit per account, applied to each bill separately, and the invoice goes to the most recently added tenant on that property.
Partners portal: partners sign in at /partners and see Dashboard, Investments, Payouts, Maintenance, Documents, Deal Analyser and Broadcast. Staff manage them in Staff Centre, Partners, Partners tab: each partner card has Investment (set the amount invested, the currency, the first repayment date and either a fixed monthly repayment or a share of monthly net income, then Save and build schedule; press Mark paid on each month, press Edit on any month to change its date or amount (or Remove it), and Add a month; the partner sees every change at once; months already paid are kept when you rebuild), Documents (upload the signed agreement and other files; hide or show each file to the partner; approve or reject files a partner uploads) and Access. Long-term (on the card: tick the property management properties this partner is in) feeds the Long term dashboard. On the Dashboard tab partners switch between Short term and Long term: Long term shows rent collected, paid on time, rent due against collected and their tenancies. Partners see Maintenance for every property linked to them: each issue shows Reported, In progress and Solved, updated from the same maintenance list staff use. Choose each partner's currency (J$, £, US$, €, CA$ or AED) in the Investment panel; amounts show in it. Limits: the repayment schedule is built from the amount and plan you enter, it does not move money; Maintenance covers both their short stay and long-term properties. Partners are listed under their own Partners group in Settings, Portal Access.
View only: in Settings, Team Management, Edit team member (and when inviting or creating someone) tick View only. In Staff Centre, Partners, Access on a partner card there is the same tick. A view-only person can open every tab and module you gave them but cannot add, edit, delete, upload or mark anything; the database and the server both refuse those changes. They can still send messages and replies (inboxes, chat, WhatsApp, SMS, guest messages, broadcasts). They see a yellow View only bar at the top. Limits: for partners it only applies when you tick extra modules or tabs for them; Novourq Cloud AI actions that change data are blocked for view-only people too.
Upkeep team: cleaning and maintenance are now one team and one portal (upkeep@thenovourq.com: property maintenance, repairs, preventative maintenance, cleaning services, housekeeping, cleaning schedules and property upkeep). Role is Upkeep Team in Settings, Team Management (the old Cleaning Team and Maintenance Team roles were merged into it with all their jobs and history kept). Upkeep staff sign in and see one My Tasks list with repairs and cleans together, filter buttons All, Repairs & maintenance and Cleaning, and a Repair or Cleaning badge on each job. Open job gives the clean checklist and photos for a clean, or Start job, photos, note, cost and Mark solved for a repair. Staff overview: Human Intelligence Hub, Portals, Upkeep shows headcount, who is on shift today, open, in progress, done this week and not assigned jobs, repair cost this month, each person with a View portal link, and the latest open jobs; the portal is also listed in Human Intelligence Hub, Portals, Portal Access as Upkeep Portal. Old cleaning and maintenance portal links open the Upkeep portal. Limits: counts cover current properties only; a job counts for a person only when assigned to them; cost is a number with no currency and does not create an invoice or expense; the clean checklist wording is the same for every property. In the staff sidebar (Operations) one Upkeep board replaces the Maintenance Board and Cleaning pages: Staff Centre, Operations, Upkeep, with a switch at the top between Repairs & maintenance and Cleaning (old links still work; the Cleaning view lists cleans from Vacation Rentals, Property Management and Estate Agency; New Task there creates a Vacation Rentals clean). Upkeep staff can open both the Maintenance and Cleaning tabs on the property pages.
Co-hosts: people who host properties they do not own and have us manage them. Find them in Human Intelligence Hub, Clients and sales, Owners & Tenants, Co-hosts (or Staff Centre, Co-hosts). Press Add co-host to enter their details, pick how we are paid (We keep a percentage, They pay us a fee, or As per contract, matching what they signed), the agreement dates and which short-stay properties we manage for them. On each card: Edit, Documents (ID, the owner's consent to host, proof of address, bank details; the co-hosting agreement is added by us), View portal and Create login (an email and password you give them). New client link lets you pick A co-host so they fill in their own details, upload documents and sign the agreement you choose; their record is created for you. When they sign in they land in the Co-host portal with Overview (properties, bookings, booking revenue and, when we keep a percentage, their share), Bookings, Maintenance (each issue at their properties from Reported to Solved), Agreement and Documents. Limits: the share shown is a simple percentage of booking revenue before any expenses; fee and per-contract arrangements show the terms only and do not calculate payouts; maintenance shown is for short-stay properties.
Bank accounts: Staff Centre, Documents, press Bank accounts at the top. Admins add or edit the company's bank accounts (bank, account name, number, branch or sort code, currency, payment reference) and mark each as Deposits (client account) or Rent and other payments; other staff can see them. In a template, the blanks Deposit bank details and Payment bank details (group Bank accounts) fill in from this list, using the tenant's currency when one matches (Jamaican properties use JMD), so changing the bank here changes every new document. Documents already sent keep the details they went out with. A switched-off account is not shown.
Tenant onboarding: Human Intelligence Hub, Clients and sales, Owners & Tenants, Tenant onboarding. It lists the pack every new tenant gets: Client information sheet, Lease agreement with security deposit scheme, Your security deposit guide, How to rent in Jamaica, Payment instructions, Tenant portal guide and Welcome letter. Press Send pack on a tenant (Property Management or Estate Agency) to give them every document they have not had; they then see them as separate items in the Onboarding tab of their portal and in Tenant onboarding on their secure link, each marked To sign, Signed or Ready, with Review and sign for the ones that need a signature (the lease asks them to initial and sign). The information sheet, lease, payment instructions and welcome letter are templates you can edit in Documents, Templates; the three PDFs are fixed files. Bank details in the lease and payment instructions fill from Documents, Bank accounts. Limits: sending the pack does not email the tenant, so tell them or send the secure link; the inventory list is not part of the pack yet; the lease text is as supplied and stops at clause 1.5, so check it with your solicitor and add the remaining clauses in the template before real use.
Staff onboarding a landlord, step by step (also in Settings → Guide, Onboard a landlord, with a picture): 1. Enquiry arrives from the landlords link or enquiry form into CRM Pipeline (Enquiry) and Landlord Leads. 2. Contact them and move the lead along. 3. Send a new client link from Human Intelligence Hub, Clients and sales, Owners & Tenants, Documents. 4. They submit the agreement and upload ID, proof of ownership, address and bank details. 5. Check them under Owners, add a co-host under Co-hosts if needed, and approve the filed documents. 6. Property Management, Landlords, Onboarding: tick the checklist, pick the manager, set agreement type and dates, Mark as onboarded.
- Smoobu connection security: the Smoobu API key and secret entered under Integrations (Property Management or Vacation Rentals) are saved encrypted, per company. Keys saved earlier are encrypted automatically within about 10 minutes, at the next Smoobu sync. Other integration keys are not encrypted yet. Nothing changes in how you connect or use Smoobu.
- Feasibility: Real Estate Intelligence → Developments → Feasibility. Tests a site before you buy it. Four ways out, shown as tabs: Land as is (hold and sell), Paper lots (get approvals, sell approved lots), Pads finished (build roads and services, sell finished plots) and Homes built (build and sell homes). Each shows profit, sales, months, margin on cost, peak cash needed, loan at its highest, return a year, profit per lot and equity multiple, as Downside, Base or Upside (the Downside and Upside shifts to prices, costs and months can be edited). Sources and uses lists every cost, equity and loan. Cost sliders (commission, closing costs, marketing, warranty, overhead, contingency, loan share, interest, HOA subsidy, city fees per lot) change profit straight away. Also: cash over time chart, comparable sales you enter (average price and price per square foot against your planned price), site facts with their sources, and pads with the soil to cut and fill, priced at your cost per cubic metre and added to site works. The 3D site shows the ground, pads, roads, houses and trees; Play or the slider shows the build month by month; Natural or Slope view (slope is colour-coded); Pads, Creek, Angle, Top down and Side cut camera buttons. Ground levels: paste survey points (x, y, height in metres) or enter the site latitude and longitude to load ground levels from a free 30 m service, which is rough and not detailed survey data. Press Save to keep a site; saved sites sit along the top, are the company's own and can be deleted. The first screen is an Example site with invented figures. Limits: it is arithmetic on the figures you enter, not advice or a valuation; the 3D houses and trees are illustrations, not a photograph of the site; ground levels from the service are rough, so use a survey for earthworks you rely on; nothing is sent anywhere.
- AI and messages: admins can ask Novourq Cloud AI (Ask AI, Novourq Voice, or the WhatsApp Phone Assistant) what has happened and what people have said, for example What came in today, Anything I need to reply to, What did the guest at the villa write, or Summarise this week's calls. It reads the latest messages from the company's channels (about 7 days): email, WhatsApp, text messages, calls with their summaries, short-stay guest messages and website chat. Only admins get this; other staff do not. Limits: staff direct messages in team chat are not included, only the latest messages are read (not the whole history), a channel that is not connected shows nothing, and the AI reads and summarises but does not reply on its own.
- Development project main image: Real Estate Intelligence → Developments → Projects → New Project or Edit → Main image (JPG, PNG or WebP). The picture shows at the top of the project card and in the side panel when the project's pin is opened on the Map (Property → Map). Remove image takes it off. Each company's images are its own. Projects without an image look as before.
- Dynamic Dossier: Real Estate Intelligence → Vacation Rentals (Short Stays) → Dynamic Dossier, under Insights, also listed under Vacation Rentals on the Property page. Suggests a nightly price for each of the next 14 nights for one short-stay property, from the company's own rules and bookings. Rates tab: enter a base price, a floor and a ceiling, plus a weekend uplift, a last-minute cut, a single-night gap cut and a busy-month uplift (each a percentage), then Save rules. Suggested prices never go below the floor or above the ceiling and each night shows why it was priced that way; booked nights show Booked. Performance tab: occupancy, average nightly rate and income for the last 30 days against the 30 before, how full the next 60 days are, and a table by property, worked out from the bookings in the portal (cancelled stays left out; a stay's total is spread evenly over its nights). Amounts use the company's own currency symbol. Rules are saved per company and per property. Listings tab: one row per short-stay property with its base price, floor and ceiling, the average suggested price for the next 14 nights, 30-day occupancy and whether rules are saved; Edit rules jumps to that property on Rates. Market tab: how full the next 60 nights are across all properties (one bar per night), which weekdays fill over the last 60 days, the typical stay length and the busiest and quietest weekday, all from the company's own bookings. Limits: prices are suggestions only and nothing is sent to Airbnb or any other channel yet, so copy them into the channel manager; there is no competitor or outside market data; it needs bookings in the portal to show results. Preview example shows labelled sample figures that are not real data.
- Scale: left menu → Scale, between Real Estate Intelligence and Novourq Cloud AI (staff with the Company Documents tab). Shows how big this company's master lease and co-host business is, from its own records only. Cards: Doors under management (head leases plus properties assigned to co-hosts), Master leases (and how many end within 90 days), Co-hosts (and properties hosted), Margin after head rent (monthly income entered on the property minus rent payable on the head lease, only where both are entered, per currency) and Co-host bookings for the last 90 days (booked stays on the properties assigned to co-hosts, cancelled bookings left out). What needs attention lists head leases past or within 90 days of expiry, head leases whose sublet consent is not Yes (Pending, verbal only or No), co-host agreements ended or ending within 90 days, and head leases with no rent entered. Growth shows doors under management at the end of each of the last 12 months, counted from lease start dates and co-host agreement start dates (or the date they were added if no start date). Master leases and Co-host management list each record, soonest end first, and pressing one opens Head Leases or Co-hosts. Preview example swaps in labelled sample figures (not real data) and Back to my data returns. Limits: figures are only as good as the records, so enter rent payable and property income to see margin; amounts are shown per currency and not converted; co-host bookings need the properties assigned to the co-host in Co-hosts and the stays to be in Bookings; it reads records and changes nothing. Everyone on the team who can open Scale sees the same company figures, and it refreshes whenever you come back to the page or press Refresh.
- Onboarding tracker: Human Intelligence Hub → Owners & Tenants → Onboarding tracker (any staff member). One board of every landlord, tenant, co-host and investor being onboarded (added in the last 120 days, or with an unfinished link; tick Include clients added more than 120 days ago for the rest), plus people who were sent a new client link and have not opened it. Each row shows a progress bar (steps done), the next step, and how many days nothing has moved. Stuck means not finished and nothing has moved for 7 days (the last move is a step ticked, the person finishing their link, or when they were added). Filter by Stuck, In progress, Not started or Finished, by Landlords, Tenants, Co-hosts or Investors, or search a name. Press a row to open its steps: steps marked automatic tick themselves from real records (ID uploaded, agreement signed from Documents, deposit protected, first rent or payment received, move-in once a signed tenancy has started, co-host portal login, marked as onboarded) and cannot be ticked by hand; agreement signed, first rent and move-in also tick themselves but staff can tick them by hand when it was done on paper; every other step is ticked by hand. Contact and link: Copy link, Remind now (emails the person their private link again, needs an email on the link and an unexpired link) and Extend 14 days (restarts the reminders). Automatic reminders: every day at 10:00 UTC a person who was sent a private link and has not finished gets an email reminder, the first after 2 days, then every 3 days, up to 4, and none after the link expires; staff also get a bell alert (at most once every 3 days) naming clients who are stuck, which opens the tracker. Limits: reminders only go to people with an email on their link; property onboarding (the 10 steps per property) is still ticked in Settings → Platform Owner → Customer Onboarding, which only the platform owner can open and which shares the same steps.
Landlord onboarding: in Property Management, Landlords tab, press Onboarding on a landlord. Tenants have the same Invite to Portal button on their row in Property Management, Tenants. Co-hosts have it too, on their row in Staff Centre, Co-hosts. Press Invite to Portal on the same row to give them their own portal: Email invite sends them a link to set their own password, or type a password yourself and share it. It shows a checklist (contact details, ID and proof of ownership, payout details, signed agreement, manager assigned, property linked, portal login) that ticks itself as things are filed, and lets you pick the landlord's named manager from your team, set the agreement type (Standard management, Guaranteed rent or Partnership), its start and end dates and the terms the landlord sees, then Mark as onboarded. The new client link in Human Intelligence Hub, Documents, is still how a new landlord first sends their details. Any staff member can send a new client link and add or edit contract templates (Documents, Templates, New template, Upload Word or PDF); a template saved by someone who is not an admin stays a draft until an admin ticks Live, and only admins can delete a template. Landlords see a Getting you set up card on their Dashboard until you mark them onboarded, plus My Manager (name, role, email, phone) and Agreement tabs in their portal; their signed copy is in Documents. Limits: one named manager per landlord; the terms are text you write, they do not calculate payments.
- Guest check-in (short lets): in Vacation Rentals, Guest Check-ins. Guests get a link by email 3 days before arrival (reminder 2 days before) and on their phone enter their details, upload a photo ID, save a card for the security deposit and sign the house rules. To switch it on, edit a property and turn on Online check-in, set the Security deposit and the Check-in terms (if empty the house rules are used). You can also press Send link on any booking. The deposit is a saved card, not a hold: nothing is charged unless you press Charge damage (never more than the deposit); Release deposit forgets the card. ID photos are private and deleted 30 days after check-out. Needs Stripe connected for the card step.
- Platform Owner section: a small section under Settings in the sidebar, shown only to the Novourq platform owner's own login (Customer Onboarding, Revenue and Customers, AI Usage and Costs, Audit Log and Notes, which has folders). Client companies, their admins and their teams never see it or the data behind it, it is not in Team Management's tick-list and cannot be granted. If someone asks about it, say it is not part of their plan's tools. Which pages are in it is set in the code (OWNER_TABS in lib/staffHubs.ts), not in Settings.
- AI Assistant: Human Intelligence Hub → AI Assistant. Tabs: Ask AI (ask Novourq Cloud AI about your records), Activity (everything the receptionist handled, with a Need follow-up filter), Channels (admins switch it on for email per mailbox, tenant and landlord messages and website chat, and choose Always or Out of hours), Knowledge & hours (receptionist name, company name, alert email, time zone, opening hours and what it knows about your company; it only states what is written here), Try it (a test chat) and Agents (the Property Manager helpers). It answers only from your Knowledge text and the customer's own property details, never changes records or makes payments, and passes anything else to staff by email alert and the Need follow-up list. Phone calls: on the Channels tab, the Phone calls card. Choose Off, When nobody answers, Out of hours or Every call. Write a Welcome message (every caller hears it first) and a Voicemail message (played before the beep). Put callers through to is your own phone number. Tick Ring my phone first to play the welcome, ring your phone, and only if you don't answer hand the caller to the AI, which talks to them, answers from the Knowledge text, takes messages and viewing requests and notes their details; if they don't speak or ask for it, they get the voicemail message and can leave a recording (up to 2 minutes), which is saved with its transcript when Twilio provides one and alerts staff. Every caller who speaks or leaves a voicemail is added to the CRM as a contact (source Phone call) with a note of the call, or a note is added if their number is already there. Leave Ring my phone first off if your own phone already forwards unanswered calls to this number, or it would ring you twice. It needs a phone number first: buy a Twilio number, type it in The phone number callers reach and save, set the number's Voice webhook in Twilio (A call comes in) to https://app.thenovourq.com/api/voice/twiml (HTTP POST), then forward your own or your Wocom number to it. Until a number is typed in, the card shows Waiting for a phone number. Limits: only admins change settings; the AI only states what is in the Knowledge text; recording links open through Twilio; transcripts may not arrive for every voicemail.
- Team access (Settings, Team Management, Edit team member): Custom module access has chips for Vacation Rentals, Property Operations & Real Estate Intelligence (one chip switches on both), Estate Agency, Developments, Staff Centre, AI Property Manager and Deal Analyser & Watchlist. Ticking Staff Centre shows a list of Human Intelligence Hub tabs to lock for that person: Dashboard, Novourq Cloud AI, Data Hub, Company Documents, Partners, Investors, Meetings, Listings, Smart Home, Conversations, Portal Access, Property Portals, Maintenance Board, Compliance, Finance, CRM, Landlord Leads, Client Properties, Invoices, Approvals, Marketing, Applications, Announcements, Activity Log, Staff Performance, People & HR, Staff Training, Calendar and Tasks. Every tab is open by default; unticking locks it and only admins can unlock it. Finance is admin-only unless ticked. Email, Airbnb Inbox, Website Chats and AI Assistant follow the Conversations tick, and Tax Compliance follows Finance. Team members work on the company's records everywhere, and anything they add (CRM, vendors, documents, properties) is saved to the company, including Marketing campaigns, emails and templates and Company Documents, and the AI helpers (lead qualify, guest reply, maintenance, cleaning, revenue) use the company name and the company's properties.
- Novourq Cloud AI as an accountant: on money, the books and tax, Novourq Cloud AI (the Ask AI chat and Novourq Voice) works like a careful property accountant. It shows its workings, labels estimates, checks the books for problems (uncategorised expenses, unmatched rent, arrears, landlord payouts that do not match what was collected), separates client money from company money, and applies the right country's rules (UK, Jamaica, UAE), looking up current rates and thresholds when web search is on. It is an AI, not a qualified accountant: VAT returns, annual accounts and tax filings should be reviewed and filed by the company's own accountant.
- Team Management (Settings): the team table scrolls sideways (scrollbar under it) and the View as, Edit and bin (remove) buttons stay pinned on the right so they are always reachable. Below the people it shows Novourq Cloud AI, the single AI that works for the whole business, with its skills (property management, rent and invoices, finance and tax, maintenance, compliance and risk, deals, inbox and reception, schedule and reviews) and when it hands over to a person. It is the same for every account and cannot be edited there. There are no named AI staff. Skills are switched on or off in AI Authority and Workflows.
- Feedback: landlords and tenants each have a Feedback tab in their own portal where they give a 1 to 5 star rating, choose what it is about and write a comment. It appears for the company in Real Estate Intelligence under Landlord Feedback or Tenant Feedback, where each item is marked New, Seen or Actioned. The team gets a bell notification for each new one. Staff can Reply from the tab: the reply shows in the person's portal Feedback tab and is emailed to them in the company's branding. People only see their own feedback. Staff previewing a portal cannot send feedback for someone. Replies are a two-way thread: when the team replies, the person gets an email and can answer from their portal's Feedback tab, which puts the item back to New. When feedback or an answer arrives, the company's owner and its Admin, Co Founder and Property Management Team members are emailed with a link.
- Rent Reviews (Real Estate Intelligence, Lettings and sales): each lease's next rent review date, current and proposed rent and status (Upcoming, Notice sent, Agreed, Declined, Done). Buttons mark the notice sent and agreed. It is a register and reminder list: it does not send the notice or change the rent. Service Charges (Finance, "Service charges and ground rent"): service charge, ground rent and sinking fund per property, who it is paid to, how often, next due date and paid status; Mark paid, then Next period moves the due date on. Planned Maintenance (Operations): recurring jobs such as boiler services and legionella flushing with next due date; Done records today and moves the next due date on by the job's frequency. It does not create repair jobs by itself. Each day Novourq Cloud AI checks Rent Reviews (due within 60 days), Service Charges (due within 2 weeks or overdue) and Planned Maintenance (due within 2 weeks or overdue) and leaves one task for each that lists them. It only lists: it never sends a notice, pays a charge or books a job. Switch each watcher on or off in Novourq Cloud AI under Agents. Emergency Contacts (Operations): plumber, electrician, gas engineer, key holder and out-of-hours numbers, for one property or all properties. Contractors (Operations) opens the contractors and suppliers page with work orders and costs.
- Connecting email and website chat (any client company can do this itself): Human Intelligence Hub, Inbox, Email, Mailbox settings. The quickest way is the Sign in with Google or Sign in with Microsoft buttons (shown on Add mailbox and on Connect): the person approves access on the provider's own page and Novourq never sees their password. These buttons only work once the platform owner has switched them on; otherwise they are greyed out and the password method is used. Password method: an admin presses Add mailbox, types the address, then Connect, and picks the provider (Gmail or Google Workspace needs an app password; Microsoft 365 or Outlook may need the Microsoft admin to allow IMAP and SMTP; website hosting such as Bluehost or cPanel uses the mailbox password; or another provider with its IMAP and SMTP server names). Passwords are stored encrypted. Website chat: Human Intelligence Hub, Inbox, Website Chats. Each company's chat settings and key are created automatically; copy the one-line code snippet into the website footer or custom code area. A mailbox signed in this way shows its sign-in expiring as Needs attention if access is withdrawn; press Reconnect and sign in again.
- Private mailboxes: a mailbox set to Private shows under Private (only you) in the Email sidebar and only the people named in its Access can open it, admins included (Mailbox settings, the Staff/Department pill).
- Novourq Cloud AI box: it now sits at the bottom of every page (the same box as the dashboard), so you can ask a question without going back. It is read only and cannot change records. It is left off the Email page.
- New applicants card: the Dashboard shows people who have just applied, each with a Reply button that opens the acceptance, decline and interview messages. It is empty when nobody new is waiting.
- AI CV review and decisions: open a candidate in Team, Applications and press Run AI review. The AI reads the CV against the role and gives a score out of 100, Strong fit, Possible or Not a fit, with reasons and things to check. It only advises, uses skills and experience (never age, gender, race, religion, health or similar) and cannot read scanned images or old .doc files. Under Your decision staff pick Invite to interview, Make an offer or Decline; that sets the stage and opens the matching message, addressed to the email the applicant applied with. Staff press Send; nothing goes automatically. If staff go against the AI it is recorded. Replies are sent from the mailbox marked Applicants in Email, Mailbox settings (NOVOURQ uses career@thenovourq.com); an admin can mark a different mailbox for their own company, and only one can be marked.
- Website careers page: the thenovourq.com careers page is a modern Current vacancies page with a map (United Kingdom, United States, Jamaica) and a job list. Set where a role is based in Open roles, Location (one or more of United Kingdom, United States, Jamaica, separated by commas; empty means all three); the map markers show how many roles are in each place. It loads its roles live from Open roles and sends applications (with CV and the location chosen) to Applications and the CRM, so the website and the portal share one list. Code is in website/careers-page.html in the repo. All staff chat: Inbox, Conversations, Message everyone opens the All staff chat; new team members are added to it automatically when an admin opens it (external partners are left out). Group and video calls: in Inbox, Conversations, Team Chat open a chat and press Group call (chats with three or more people) for a voice call, or Video call for video with camera and screen share. A message appears in the chat with a Join call button, so everyone in the chat can join from the portal instead of their mobile; calls last up to 3 hours and only people in that chat can join. It needs DAILY_API_KEY set in Netlify (a Daily account); until then the buttons say calling is not switched on. Calls run on the platform owner's Daily account. The platform owner's own company is unlimited; a client company only gets them when the platform owner sets a monthly allowance of participant minutes (one person in a call for one minute) in Platform Owner, Revenue and Customers, Call minutes this month (0 means off). That column shows minutes used this month and the Daily cost so you can charge for it. When a company reaches its allowance no new call can start or be joined until you raise it; a call already running is not cut off.
- Email on a phone: Human Intelligence Hub, Inbox, Email shows one thing at a time on a phone. The list of emails fills the screen; tap one to read it, then Back to Inbox to return. Folders opens the folders, mailboxes, Email templates and Mailbox settings menu, and + New writes a new email.
- Real Estate Intelligence is one place for property management, estate agency, short stays (vacation rentals) and developments. Open it, search any page or pick an area, and use "← Real Estate Intelligence" to go back. Every tab has a blue banner saying what it does.
- At a glance (bottom of the Real Estate Intelligence page): four rows of headline tiles, one row each for Short term rentals, Lettings, Estate agency and Developments, showing only the areas the person can open. Short term rentals: occupancy for the next 30 days, revenue this month with the last 6 months, check-ins in the next 7 days and guest rating. Lettings: rent collected this month, arrears, empty units and open repairs. Estate agency: live listings, viewings in the next 7 days, vacancies and open repairs. Developments: budget spent, milestones due in 14 days, snags open and units sold. Each tile opens its page. It is read only and uses records already in Novourq. Estate agency has no offers or sales pipeline records yet, so it shows none.
- Human Intelligence Hub lists every people-run area (inbox, CRM, finance, reports, operations, team) grouped under headings, with a search box. At the top, the Where do I go? card lists everyday tasks (reply to a customer, follow up a lead, chase rent, pay an owner, raise an invoice, log a repair, manage staff and more); each task has buttons that open the right page. It only shows pages your role can open. At the bottom, At a glance shows what needs you today as number tiles in the same four groups: unread messages, website chats, CRM follow-ups due, viewing requests, approvals waiting, overdue rent payments, partner payments to confirm, open repairs, certificates expiring within 30 days, meetings, tasks due, applications to review, staff requests and unread announcements. They are the same counts as the red badges on the menu, each tile opens the page it comes from, and a tile only shows if your role can open that page. They show counts, not money amounts.
- Editing: records on every page have an Edit button (leases, units, maintenance, expenses and so on). Summary pages (Deadlines, Finance overview, Audit Log) are read-only.
- Novourq Cloud AI front page (Novourq Cloud AI in the left menu): a Where do I go? card of everyday tasks (approve drafts, switch a skill on, run every skill now, plan my day and more) that opens the right page, a search box, headings (Control, Skills, Automation, Insight, Tools) with each page and a line on what it does, then At a glance (waiting for approval, skills switched on, sent in 30 days, hours saved), today's briefing, skills running and latest alerts. Inside any page the side menu has ← Novourq Cloud AI at the top to return. It only opens pages; nothing is changed from the front page.
- Rent by Direct Debit: a Property Management tenant paying rent from their portal can choose Bacs Direct Debit as well as card. Rent stays unpaid until the money clears (a few days), then marks itself paid with method direct debit. It needs Bacs Direct Debit switched on in the business's Stripe account and the checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded event sent to the webhook; if Bacs is not on, the tenant just sees card. Estate Agency rent is card only for now.
- Novourq Cloud AI is the one AI that runs the platform. It has skills (not separate staff). Each skill watches a part of the business, writes the message or task, and sends or hands it over. See Novourq Cloud AI → Skills, Workflows, Approvals and Results.
- What the AI does without asking: sends emails, replies, instructions, price changes, listings, rent matching and imports. At most 40 automatic actions a day per business. Each skill has a "Send automatically" tick box on its page in Skills; untick it to approve that skill's messages yourself.
- What always needs a person for now: anything that sends money, and legal contracts (lease changes, renewal offers, signing). The one exception: an admin can ask Novourq Voice to email test contracts to their own address. Those wait in Approvals (Novourq Cloud AI → Approvals). The AI cannot send money.
- Run now: Novourq Cloud AI → Workflows → "Run all now" runs every switched-on skill immediately. Otherwise they run daily at 07:30 UTC (some weekly on Mondays or monthly on the 1st).
- Rent reminders: sent by email and to the tenant's portal (never texts). Windows: 7 to 4 days before, 3 to 1 days before, due day, 1 to 2 days late, 3 to 6 late, 7 to 13 late, 14 to 20 late, 21 or more late. One message per window per rent; skipped if the rent is paid. See Human Intelligence Hub → Finance → Reminders. Arrears list: Human Intelligence Hub → Finance → Arrears, or Real Estate Intelligence → Property Management → Rent.
- Email branding: every AI email uses the company's own logo, name and contact footer, and replies go to their reply-to address. Set these in Human Intelligence Hub → Finance → Invoices → "Invoice settings" (admin only): company name, logo upload, contact lines (address, phone, email, one per line), reply-to. Without them the email shows just the company name.
- Website chat button: on the Novourq website the chat button is the light blue Novourq Voice pill with the animated Novourq mark; other companies keep their own assistant name. The name shown comes from Website Chats → Settings & install.
- WhatsApp Business in the Inbox: each company connects its own number in Settings, WhatsApp (admins only): press Connect with Facebook, or paste the Phone number ID, WhatsApp Business Account ID and access token from Meta. It uses Meta's WhatsApp Cloud API directly, so no Twilio is needed. Once connected, a WhatsApp button appears in Human Intelligence Hub, Inbox, Conversations; any team member can read and reply there. WhatsApp only allows free-text replies for 24 hours after the customer last wrote; after that an amber bar asks for the name of an approved template (made in Meta WhatsApp Manager), which is the only thing that can be sent. In the same Settings tab an admin can tick Let Novourq Cloud AI answer on this number, choose Always or Only when the office is closed, and add a greeting and extra information. The AI uses the AI Receptionist knowledge and opening hours, replies in the chat, and shows as Novourq Cloud AI. It hands over by itself for money, contracts, complaints, emergencies or anything it cannot answer: it tells the customer a person will reply, stops answering that chat and alerts staff by bell, push and email. A red bar then shows A person has this chat. When a team member replies or presses Take over the AI also stops; Hand back to AI switches it on again for that chat. What it may send alone follows Settings, AI Authority; if replies there are set to wait for a person, nothing is sent and the suggested reply shows in the red bar. Limits: pictures, voice notes and documents show as a placeholder (open WhatsApp on the phone to view them); the AI answers text messages only; Meta business verification is needed before many numbers can message customers.
- Website chat: Novourq Cloud AI answers website visitors, saves leads and books viewings (Human Intelligence Hub → Inbox → Website Chats). A booked viewing is confirmed by email.
- Careers page and open roles: Human Intelligence Hub → Team → Applications → Open roles & careers link (top right). Add a role with title, category, location, type and description, switch it on, then Copy link and send it to candidates. The page lists your open roles; they pick one, fill in name, email, phone and a message, and submit. The application lands in Applications at Applied, the person is added to CRM as an applicant, and the team gets an email. Hide or delete a role to take it off the page. Limits: candidates can attach a CV (PDF or Word, up to 5 MB); it shows in the CV link column on the application and as an Open CV link in the team email; the careers link is separate from the website careers form below.
- Website careers form: a careers page on your own website can send job applications to Novourq. Each application appears in Human Intelligence Hub → Team → Applications at the Applied stage, with a bell alert and an email to your team, and the applicant is also added to Human Intelligence Hub → CRM as a contact (type applicant, source Website careers). No deal is created, because an applicant is not a sale. The form is set up with your website key from Inbox → Website Chats → Settings & install. Reply to candidate: open a candidate and choose Acceptance, Decline or Interview invite. The wording is generated with their name and the role (the decline thanks them for their interest and says you will not be moving forward). Edit it, press Open in my email and send it yourself, or Copy; Set stage to moves them to Offered, Rejected or Interviewing. Limits: the portal does not send it for you, and it needs the candidate's email.
- Tenants and landlords have their own portals; reminders and replies appear in the tenant portal chat.
- Setup the platform needs from the account owner: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (AI), CRON_SECRET (scheduled runs), RESEND_API_KEY (email) in Netlify. If an email or AI feature does nothing, that is the first thing to check.
- Novourq Cloud AI's picture: the Novourq symbol as a glossy 3D mark on a blue glow, with a small blue light. On the AI pages and the Dashboard AI panel it plays as a short looping animation. The Voice button is a light blue pill with the blue logo animating on it, with no box behind it. Phones set to reduce motion show the still picture.
- Novourq Voice: the navy "Novourq Voice" pill at the bottom right of every page. Press it to start a phone-style call with the AI: say what you want and it does it (add a task, log a repair, add a contact, draft an email, find deals, open any page). The small pencil button next to it types what you say into whatever box you have open (dictation, with filler words removed). The speaker button turns the AI's spoken replies on or off. Staff can say "Novourq, ..." on any page to give an instruction. Hotkey for dictation: Ctrl+Shift+Space. It works on phones in the browser (keep the screen on). It asks before anything that sends money or a contract, and emails it drafts wait in Approvals. Settings → Voice: choose a Woman or Man voice, add your own dictionary words and shortcuts, and read or delete past call transcripts. It only works inside Novourq, not in other apps. Realistic voice needs the OpenAI (or ElevenLabs) key set; otherwise the phone's built-in voice is used.
- Tenants and landlords also get Novourq Voice in their portal as a personal assistant. It only sees that person's own records. A tenant can report a repair (it appears in Maintenance), message the agent or ask for a document; a landlord can message the agent or request a service. It cannot pay, change a tenancy or lease, or share anything about other people.
- Data Hub: Human Intelligence Hub → Oversight → Data Hub (admin only). Shows counts of properties, tenants, landlords and documents, a data-health score with what to fix, where the data came from (import, AI, staff), recent AI changes, and requests from tenants and landlords to download, correct or delete their data (with Complete and Decline buttons). Tenants and landlords see their own "My Data" tab in their portal: a summary, downloadable copy, and requests to correct or delete.
- Map: Real Estate Intelligence → Overview → Map. A street map of every property and found deal, coloured by status: green let, blue vacant, red rent behind, amber certificate due, purple diamond deal found, teal In development (your Development projects, placed from the project's Location). Filters for each status and for UK or Jamaica. Click a pin for tenant, rent, overdue payments and certificates, and a button to open the property. Positions are looked up from the address once and saved; a property that is missing from the map usually has an address that could not be found, so check it. A smaller version of the map is on the Dashboard and the Business snapshot. The "3D" button switches to a tilted 3D city with real buildings (free OpenStreetMap data, so UK city centres are good and Jamaica is patchier); the property's own building is raised in its status colour; click a property in the list to fly to it. You can also say "open the map" to the voice agent.
- Floors, floor plans and walk-through: on the Map page, click a pin for a property in a building and press "View floors". The tower shows every flat by floor, coloured let, vacant or rent behind, with its rent. Floors come from the flat's saved floor, or from its number (3B is floor 3, 204 is floor 2). Click a flat for tenant, rent and status. "Add floor plan" uploads a PNG, JPG, WEBP or PDF plan; "Read plan with AI" turns it into rooms (the AI uses one rectangle per room, so check the sizes) or you draw the rooms on a grid; "Save rooms" keeps them. Then "View in 3D and walk" opens a furnished 3D model of the flat with three buttons: Plan (turn the model), Walk (first-person walk-through) and Tour (starts outside: a person crosses the road and walks up to the building entrance, with surrounding blocks, trees and palms, then it cuts inside and the person walks through every room in turn while the camera follows from above, with the room name shown; rooms have textured floors, detailed furniture and a few other people; it loops). "Save as video" runs the tour once and downloads it as a video file (MP4 or WEBM depending on the browser) with the building name, room names and the Novourq mark on it, ready to share. The building outside is a generic sample block named after your building, not a model of the real one, and the 3D is simple shapes, not photographs. The Walk mode is a first-person walk-through (arrow keys or WASD, drag to look, joystick on phones). It is simple 3D built from the plan, not photographs. The flats must be linked to a building (Property Management → Buildings) for the floors view to appear. Development showcase: Development projects are on the same Map as teal pins. Select one and press View floors to see its units (Development → Units) by floor, coloured Available, Reserved or exchanged, or Sold, with the price on each. Click a unit for buyer, price and details, add its floor plan, read it with AI and open it in 3D to walk through before it is built, which is how to show investors and buyers what is coming. A unit's floor comes from its number (204 is floor 2, 3B is floor 3). A project only gets a pin once its Location can be found. It is staff-only for now; the investor portal does not show it.
- HR Documents: Human Intelligence Hub → Team → HR Documents (Admin and HR Team only). A file library for payslips, HR forms, HR contracts and employee records. Add NOVOURQ templates adds the fillable payslip, the proof of employment letter and the Work Hours staff notice (what Work Hours records, why, who sees it, with a signature line for the employee). Add document uploads a file; Open / fill in opens it; Edit renames, moves or replaces it with a completed copy; Send emails the file to a person with a subject and message; Delete is Admin only. Company Documents in Staff Centre has the same Edit and Send buttons for company papers. HR templates: Staff Centre → Documents → Templates → Add HR templates (admins) adds an editable Payslip, Proof of employment letter, the Work Hours staff notice and an Offer letter for each role (Receptionist, CEO, COO, CPMO, CFO, CTO, CDO, CCO, CRO: job title, start date, pay, hours, holiday, probation, notice, confidentiality, with an employee signature) that take the company's own logo, name and contact lines from Invoice settings; pick a person, fill the blanks (salary, hours, holiday, notice), send by link so the new hire can view and sign. Every offer letter has the NOVOURQ artwork as its page background on the signing page and the PDF. Offer letter emails show career@thenovourq.com in the footer and replies go to it, and the email subject fills in the company name; the new hire opens the link from the email, types their own home address and any other blanks left for them, and signs. Fill the company address, work location and your role yourself before sending. Offer letters are general wording, not legal advice; have a lawyer check them for where you employ. In those the payslip amounts are typed, not calculated. Limits: HR files never show on Company Documents or to other staff; fillable PDFs are completed in the viewer then re-uploaded; calculated fields only work in Adobe Acrobat.
- Tenant checks from the tenant link: a tenant uploads their photo ID, right to rent result, proof of income, bank statements and references on their link (New client link, Tenant). Novourq Cloud AI reads the ID, right to rent, income and bank statement files and saves what it saw. Open Property Management → Compliance → Tenant Checks, press Add Checks (or Edit) on their lease, and a blue box shows what the AI read with a Fill the form from these button. Staff then check it against the documents and set Passed or Failed themselves, the AI never decides. Limits: photos or PDFs only, files over 8 MB are not read, blurry scans can come back with gaps, the right to rent share code is not checked against the Home Office, and the tenant needs a lease before the box shows. Estate Agency tenants are not read yet.
- Services Pack: Staff Centre → Marketing → Services Pack. Holds the documents we send to show our services (welcome page, brochure, landlord pack, flyers). The website popup's Find out more button asks for an email and a tick to agree to marketing emails, then saves the person in the CRM (contact plus a deal at Enquiry, consent noted in the notes) and alerts the team; they are marked as opted in, and you can email them all from Marketing, Emails, Mailing list. The Company brochure is 12 pages and includes pages on the AI dashboard and how the technology removes human error, and on the owners portal. Under 1. Choose what to send, press the Landlord, Co-host or Tenant tab: it shows only that audience's documents and ticks the right ones for you (each includes the Welcome page and that audience's portal guide); the All documents tab shows everything. You can untick or tick others yourself, give the link a name and press Create link. The link (/s/…) opens a branded page with the company's logo where the recipient chooses each document to view or download, no login. The Landlord tab also ticks the Welcome letter and Shortlet landlord onboarding form. The Landlord tab also ticks the Landlord detail sheet (fillable: up to four landlords on page 1 and the property on page 2; a completed copy is filed on that landlord’s record under Documents and in Submitted documents, and when the link was for a new landlord they are registered and their property is created from page 2). The Tenant tab ticks the Welcome page, Welcome letter, Furnished apartments, Tenants portal guide, Tenant deposit guide, How to rent in Jamaica and the Client onboarding sheet (fillable, up to four tenants); the Tenancy agreement (fillable, in the NOVOURQ look) is there to tick when you are ready. Choose A new tenant (registered when they submit) under Who is this link for and the tenant is registered from the sheet, their completed copy and uploaded documents are filed on their record, and you press Invite to Portal on their row in Property Management, Tenants to email them a link to set their own password. The Co-host tab also has the Corporate residential partnership agreement (fillable, the co-host agreement with fee and funds options) to tick instead of or as well as the Shortlet co-host agreement. The landlord Agreements (Master Lease, Estate agency) are never ticked for you: choose the one that fits the landlord before you create the link. The Co-host tab ticks the Shortlet co-host agreement and the Cohost detail sheet (page 1 for up to four co-hosts, page 2 for the property: a new co-host and their property are created when they submit, and co-hosts 2 to 4 are registered too) (fillable like the others). The agreements and onboarding form open as fillable pages on the link: the landlord clicks the shaded boxes to type or tick, enters their name and presses Submit to NOVOURQ, and it comes straight back to you. Each link in 3. Your links shows its NOVOURQ welcome message with the link under it, and Copy message copies it (the same welcome wording on every link), and the New client link message uses the same wording (with the 14 day validity). Find completed copies under Marketing, Services Pack, 3. Submitted documents and press Open completed PDF. To make another PDF fillable online, press Edit on it and tick Recipients fill this in online (the PDF must have form fields). After submitting, a landlord or co-host linked to a record sees Upload your documents: Landlord ID, Proof of ownership, Proof of address and Bank details for a landlord (ID, Owner’s consent, Proof of address and Bank details for a co-host), each as a PDF or photo up to 15 MB. They are filed on the same record in Documents, awaiting your approval, and you get a notification. Uploads only work right after submitting a form on that link. The Property (optional) box when you create a link is a drop-down of the properties in your portfolio (Property Management, Estate Agency and Vacation Rentals), with Not listed, type it for any other; the property you choose shows at the top of the recipient’s page; the New client link in Documents has its own Property (optional) box too, so a property can be added either way. It is a label only, it does not create or pick a property. Limits: no signature box yet, so signing still happens separately; the team (owner, admins, co-founders and the Property Management Team) is emailed with the completed PDF attached each time one arrives. To file it on a person’s record, choose Who is this link for? when you create the link: A new landlord or A new co-host (they are registered from the name and email they enter when they submit, or matched by email if they already exist; the Landlord and Co-host tabs pick this for you), or An existing landlord or co-host (search by name). Which section they go in follows the agreement they submit: the Estate agency agreement creates the landlord in Estate Agency, the Master Lease creates them in Property Management, and the Shortlet co-host agreement or any co-host link creates a co-host (no property). If the form has a property address, the property is created too and linked to them (with bedrooms and bathrooms when filled in); it is skipped when the address is blank or the same property already exists for that landlord. Each submission is then also added to their Documents (Management agreement for a landlord, Co-hosting agreement for a co-host, Other documents for the onboarding form), waiting for you to approve it in Staff Centre, Human Intelligence Hub, Documents. Links with no person picked only keep the copy in Submitted documents. Links stay live until paused or deleted. Each link shows opens, last opened and views per document. Edit a document or replace its PDF and every link already sent shows the new version. Copy message gives ready wording with the link under it. Limits: PDF files only; phones sometimes won't show the PDF in the page, so there is an Open / download button; it does not insert itself into campaign emails, paste the link in.
- Training and staff: Human Intelligence Hub → Team (People & HR, Staff Performance, Staff Training, Applications, Announcements).
- Picture library: Human Intelligence Hub → Marketing → Marketing → Picture library (left list, or the Picture library button on the Marketing home page). It works exactly like the Video library but holds pictures only (JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 500 MB): press + Add picture, then fill in title, caption, hashtags, platforms, status and post time.
- Video library: Human Intelligence Hub → Marketing → Video library (left list, or the Video library button on the Marketing home page). Each company keeps its own marketing videos here; no other company can see them. Press + Add video, choose an MP4, MOV or WebM video up to 500 MB, give it a title, caption and hashtags, tick the platforms it is for (Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, X, Snapchat, LinkedIn, YouTube), set the status (Draft, Ready, Scheduled, Posted) and an optional planned post time, then Upload and save. Press a video to play it and edit its details. To post: press Download file, press Copy post text (caption followed by hashtags), post it on each platform yourself, then tick each platform under Posting. It marks the video Posted when every planned platform is ticked. Limits: the portal does not post to Instagram, TikTok, X or Snapchat for you yet, and the planned post time is only a reminder. Anyone on the team can add and edit; only an admin or the person who added a video can delete it. Novourq Cloud AI can add pictures for you: in the Novourq Cloud AI chat (at the bottom of every page, or NOVOURQ Ecosystem → Novourq Cloud AI) press the picture button next to the message box, choose up to 10 JPG, PNG or WebP pictures (under 20 MB each), optionally type what they are for (name a platform such as Instagram or TikTok to tick it), then press Send. Each picture is saved as a Draft in the Picture library with a title, caption and hashtags the AI writes after looking at it, so check them before you post.
- Mailing list: Staff Centre → Marketing → Emails → Mailing list button (top right, next to Sending as). Shows how many contacts have opted in to marketing emails and how many of each type (landlord, investor and so on); See who is on the list shows each person's name, email, where they signed up and the date. Choose the audience (Everyone or one type), then press Generate NOVOURQ message for the ready-written message about our management service (the same message for everyone, or pick a saved draft, or write your own; {{first_name}} becomes each person's first name) and edit the subject and wording. Under Documents to include (grouped as AI platform, then Property management), tick any Services Pack documents (Company brochure, AI platform brochure, Lease your property to us, Furnished apartments, Vacation rental landlord pack and others). Send documents as: Pictures in the email plus a PDF button (recommended, because many people never open PDFs), Pictures only, or PDF button only. The marketing documents have page pictures (the brochures and landlord pack show every page, flyers one); a document you upload yourself has no pictures and goes as a PDF button. Press Send to N and confirm; every email carries an unsubscribe link and a record of it is kept in Emails as Sent. Opted in means the contact ticked the marketing box on the website popup, the website sign-up form or the enquiry form, or you earlier recorded it; nobody else is emailed. When someone presses Unsubscribe (in the email, or their mail app's unsubscribe button) they are switched to not opted in straight away and never get another bulk send. The same window has the Sign-up form for your website: copy the code and paste it where the form should appear (WordPress: a Custom HTML block); sign-ups save into your own company's CRM as opted in and the person gets a thank-you email with an unsubscribe link. Novourq Cloud AI can also prepare it: ask it, for example, to send the marketing email to the mailing list with the brochure; it puts the email in Staff Centre → AI Command Centre → AI Approvals (audience everyone, landlord or investor; documents by name; pictures, PDF or both) and a person opens it, checks the wording and number of people and presses Approve, and only then is it sent. It never sends from the chat, and this approval cannot be switched to automatic in Settings → AI Authority. People who sign up through a form with data-interest="platform" (the AI platform, not landlord services) are tagged platform in the CRM and appear as their own audience in the Mailing list, so you can email them separately from landlords. For the platform audience, Generate NOVOURQ message writes a different message about the AI platform (available now, with the sign-up link and the AI platform brochure) and ticks the AI platform brochure; every other audience gets the management-service message. Anyone who creates a portal account (Start free trial) is saved in the NOVOURQ CRM as a platform lead; they join the Mailing list only if they ticked "Email me NOVOURQ product news and offers" on the sign-up form (never pre-ticked), so everyone on the list has agreed to it. Limits: it sends one at a time so a very large list takes a few minutes; there is no scheduling, no per-person personalisation yet and no list of who unsubscribed other than the contact's record; the one-off Send now on a single email is separate and has no unsubscribe link.
- Enquiry form link: Marketing (home page) → Enquiry form link card → Copy link (or Open). Send it to landlords and investors; they pick Guaranteed Rent, Short Let Partnership or Estate Property Management, fill in their details and properties and submit, and get a confirmation email. Each enquiry becomes a CRM contact (type landlord) and a deal at the Enquiry stage in the Pipeline, with all answers in the notes, and the team gets an alert. Admins can switch the link off. The same card also has One link for all landlords (app.thenovourq.com/landlords/…): existing landlords sign in to the owners portal and new ones open the enquiry form, so you only share one link; it follows the same on/off switch. It also has One link for all tenants (app.thenovourq.com/tenants): existing tenants go to the tenants portal and people looking for a home go to the property listings. It also has One link for representatives (app.thenovourq.com/representatives/…): staff sign in to the oversight portal, agents sign in to the agent portal and new agents sign up. Limits: one link per company; five enquiries a day per email address.
- Links to send people (all on app.thenovourq.com): Properties for rent (the whole stock): /homes, copy it at Staff Centre → Marketing → Listings tab → Copy link; each property also has its own Copy button. Landlords and investors who want to work with us (Guaranteed Rent, Short Let Partnership, Estate Property Management): the enquiry form, Staff Centre → Marketing → Enquiry form link → Copy link; it lands in CRM Pipeline at Enquiry. Job candidates: the careers page, Staff Centre → Human Intelligence Hub → Team → Applications → Open roles & careers link → Copy link; they apply with a CV and it lands in Applications and CRM (applicant). Landlord portals: /pm-owner-portal (Property Management), /estate-owner-portal (Estate Agency), /owner-portal (Vacation Rentals owners). Tenant portals: /pm-tenant-portal (Property Management), /estate-tenant-portal (Estate Agency). The portal links are in Staff Centre → Human Intelligence Hub → Portal Access and Settings → Portal Access. Limits: a landlord or tenant can only sign in once they have a portal login on their record; the bare link opens the sign-in page, and staff who open it see a picker.
- Agent portal: agents have their own portal at /agent-portal. Send a new agent the sign-up link (Staff Centre → Partners & Investors → Partners → Agent Programme → Agents → Agent sign-up link → Copy link). They enter name, contact, country, payout details and a password; their account then waits as paused. Press Activate on their row to approve them, and check their commission rates with Edit. Approved agents sign in at the agent portal link (same place, Copy link) and see their code, what is due, pending and paid, and each guest or tenant with its status; the top shows Three ways to earn: A Place a renter (someone who needs a fully furnished home), B Send a guest, and C List a property with us (a property they own or look after, handed to us to let), each with a Log one button, then a How it works strip (log, we screen, approved, you get paid); what they log lands in the Referral pipeline at Logged and alerts the team. Staff still set screening status and mark commission paid. Leaderboard: every approved agent sees a Leaderboard at the top of the agent portal ranking all of your company's active agents by confirmed commission; others appear as first name and initial with a relative bar, never amounts, and the agent sees their own position. Only your own company's agents are ranked. The Dashboard also shows two Agent leaderboard boxes under Automation by area: the staff view with names and commission amounts, and what agents see (first name and initial with a bar, no amounts). Website pricing: the prices on the website come from a two-line snippet (a div with id novourq-pricing plus a script loading https://app.thenovourq.com/pricing.js). It reads the live Stripe prices behind the monthly, one-time and founding-client plans, so the website always shows what Stripe charges, and Choose plan opens Stripe Checkout where the client signs up and pays. Change a price in Stripe and the website updates within a couple of minutes. Limits: agents only see their own referrals; agents never see your commission rates: a guest or tenant shows 'Commission to be confirmed' until you set the amount on that referral (Referral pipeline, open it and set the commission amount), and only amounts you have set count in their due, pending and paid totals; they cannot change anything or mark anything paid; agents can switch the amounts they see between pound, US dollar, Jamaican dollar, euro, dirham and Canadian dollar (converted from pounds at the day's rate, display only; commission is still agreed and paid in pounds, and the booking value they log is in pounds); you can still add agents yourself with Add agent. Staff can also create an agent's login themselves: Agent Programme → Agents → Add agent (or Edit), fill in the name and email, type a password of 8 or more characters in the Agent portal login box and press Save agent; that creates the login, activates the agent and they sign in at the agent portal with that email and password (for an agent who already has a login the same box sets a new password). To record money an agent has already made, press Log guest / tenant in the Referral pipeline, choose the agent, add the booking value (or monthly rent) and the Commission earned, and say whether it is already paid; it then counts in that agent's Paid or Owed. Agents only see amounts you set.
- Agent recruitment page on the website: the agent page on thenovourq.com has a form that sends each applicant to Staff Centre → CRM as a contact (type agent, source Agent page) with a deal at Enquiry in the Pipeline, alerts the team and emails the applicant a link to create their agent portal login (the agent sign-up link). The form posts to /api/public/agent-lead using the company link code. To put the page on a website, paste a two-line snippet into an Elementor HTML widget: a div with id novourq-agent and a script loading https://app.thenovourq.com/agent-page.js (this avoids the host firewall blocking a large pasted page). Limits: five applications a day per email address.
- Virtual viewings: Marketing → Listings → press a property → Virtual viewing videos (under the photos). Upload walk-through videos or paste a YouTube or Vimeo link, add a title, press Save. Tenants watch them on the property's public page (/homes) under Virtual viewing, and the viewing form has a tick box 'I cannot visit in person. Please arrange a video call', which reaches the viewings list with that note at the start of the message. Limits: it is video you film yourself, not an automatic 3D model of the property; very large video files may be refused, so use an unlisted YouTube link instead; the 3D flat walk-through on the Map is separate and is for flats with saved rooms.
- Staff Training (Human Intelligence Hub, Team) opens on Portal guides: every tab has a how-to with steps, pictures and video, a search, area filters, and a What's new box listing recent portal changes with a NEW tag until marked read. New tabs appear automatically with a Basic guide. Admins add pictures and videos per tab (upload, or paste a YouTube or Vimeo link); without one, the matching area video from the Help Centre shows. Company training (PDFs, files, videos with tick-off) is the second button. Staff who are stuck should look here first.
`

export function portalGuide(): string {
  const hubs = STAFF_HUBS.map(h => `- ${h.label}: ${h.tabs.filter(t => !t.hidden).map(t => t.label).join(', ') || '(single page)'}`).join('\n')
  const tabs = Object.entries(TAB_DESCRIPTIONS).map(([k, v]) => `- ${k.includes(':') ? k.replace(':', ' ') : k}: ${v}`).join('\n')
  const skills = WORKFLOWS.map(w => `- ${w.label} (${w.module}; ${w.schedule})`).join('\n')
  return `PORTAL GUIDE\n${HOW_TO}\nHUMAN INTELLIGENCE HUB AND OTHER MENU ITEMS (menu item: pages)\n${hubs}\n\nREAL ESTATE INTELLIGENCE TABS (what each does; "dev", "str" prefixes mean the developments and short-stay versions)\n${tabs}\n\nNOVOURQ CLOUD AI SKILLS (${WORKFLOWS.length})\n${skills}\n`
}
